{
  "ranking": [
    {
      "id": "patch_68c4a4d1add9",
      "failure_port": "output_axis_tdata",
      "source_line": 5126,
      "mechanism": "The output domain always initializes data_out_reg to 0 via its registered initial value. On reset, output_rst_sync3 asserts but the block at line 5126 contains no reset assignment for data_out_reg, so it keeps its stale memory contents and immediately outputs garbage instead of 0. Adding the missing reset drive at line 5126 forces data_out_reg to 0 during reset, making output_axis_tdata cycle-exact 0 as the trace expects."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_74df60f23eb4",
      "failure_port": "input_axis_tready",
      "source_line": 3650,
      "mechanism": "input_axis_tready is a direct combinational read of ~full. The trace expects input_axis_tready=0 at cycle 4 while async_rst=0, meaning the FIFO must appear full during reset. The readiness gate at line 3650 lacks any reset term, so ~full becomes 1 the instant async_rst de-asserts. Adding the input_rst_sync3 qualifier keeps ~full gated off until the three-stage input reset pipeline (input_rst_sync1/2/3) has fully cleared, matching the first-mismatch cycle."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_5da527582759",
      "failure_port": "output_axis_tdata",
      "source_line": 5143,
      "mechanism": "The read-domain block at line 5143 updates rd_ptr and data_out_reg when (read) is true. During reset, output_rst_sync3 asserts but the condition lacks a reset gate, so read can fire early and load garbage from mem into data_out_reg before the pointers have cleared. Qualifying the condition with (input_rst_sync3) keeps the read path disabled until the input-side reset has also completed, preventing the early wrong data at cycles 8 and 9."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_9425e1a524ed",
      "failure_port": "output_axis_tdata",
      "source_line": 4532,
      "mechanism": "The write-domain block at line 4532 pushes input data into mem and advances wr_ptr when (write) is true. During reset, async_rst de-asserts before input_rst_sync3 clears, so write can become active while the pointers are still stale, corrupting mem. Adding (input_rst_sync3) to the write condition blocks any write until the three-stage input reset has fully cleared, protecting the FIFO contents and therefore the subsequent read data."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_000305187b49",
      "failure_port": "input_axis_tready",
      "source_line": 3650,
      "mechanism": "Alternative reset gating for the readiness combinational path. Adding (!async_rst) directly to the input_axis_tready qualification keeps ~full gated off for the entire duration that async_rst is asserted, which also forces input_axis_tready=0 at cycle 4. This is a broader but still cycle-exact fix for the same first-mismatch port."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_e4d895e08cad",
      "failure_port": "input_axis_tready",
      "source_line": 3650,
      "mechanism": "Alternative reset gating using the three-stage input reset pipeline. Adding (!input_rst_sync3) to the readiness gate keeps input_axis_tready low until input_rst_sync3 de-asserts, producing the same cycle-4 zero as the trace requires."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_eb843a3e7514",
      "failure_port": "output_axis_tdata",
      "source_line": 5067,
      "mechanism": "The block at line 5067 synchronizes wr_ptr_gray into the read domain. Its reset condition only checks output_rst_sync3, so it can sample wr_ptr_gray while the write domain is still in reset (input_rst_sync3 asserted), propagating stale gray codes that make empty/full evaluate incorrectly and cause early reads. Qualifying with (!input_rst_sync3) blocks this cross-domain sync until both domains are out of reset."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_f09094005ed7",
      "failure_port": "output_axis_tdata",
      "source_line": 4532,
      "mechanism": "Alternative write-domain reset gate. Adding (!output_rst_sync3) to the write condition blocks writes until the read-domain reset has also cleared, providing symmetric cross-domain reset protection that prevents the early memory corruption seen at cycles 8 and 9."
    }
  ],
  "explanation": "The three observed mismatches cluster on two ports: input_axis_tready at cycle 4 (expected 0, got 1) and output_axis_tdata at cycles 8 and 9 (expected 2, got 3). The root causes are incomplete reset gating across clock domains. The input_axis_tready combinational path lacks any reset term, so it goes high as soon as async_rst drops. The write and read pointer updates (lines 4532 and 5143) can fire during the reset handshake before both domains have synchronized, corrupting memory and producing wrong output data. The data_out_reg register also misses its explicit reset assignment (line 5126). The ranked patches each add a minimal reset qualification that blocks the offending path until the appropriate multi-stage reset pipeline has fully cleared, restoring cycle-exact trace agreement."
}
